Article 4 The "serious circumstances" as provided in Article 320 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China shall include any of the following circumstances:
(1) Providing others with five or more forged or altered passports, visas, or other entry-exit certificates, or selling five or more passports, visas, or other entry-exit certificates;
(2) Illegally obtaining 300,000 yuan or more in proceeds;
(3) Having other serious circumstances.

Article 5 The "serious circumstances" as provided in Article 322 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China shall include any of the following circumstances where a person illegally crosses the national border (frontier):
(1) Engaging in acts that harm the interests of the State abroad;
(2) Illegally crossing the national border (frontier) three times or more;
(3) Soliciting or enticing others to illegally cross the national border (frontier) together;
(4) Illegally crossing the national border (frontier) again within one year after having been subjected to an administrative penalty for illegally crossing the national border (frontier);
(5) Having other serious circumstances.
